tags: tunnel-open, tunnel_open_mu

A rate of the node: the price of one ServiceTunnel that the node opens.

The value is MU for one. Example: 1000. The node takes it from the balance that
pays for the action.

The rate has no scope. A reader that does not know the rate ignores it.

=== formal
base=one
class=rate
name=tunnel-open
of=one ServiceTunnel stream that the node opens to an instance
scope=none
